            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KRANEY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Awesome!! \"Prepared mustard\" is dijon mustard. For the salt &amp; pepper amounts, I used 1/4 tsp. each. For the garlic powder, I used 1/8 tsp. Thanks so much for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2014-05-22T07:53:38.080Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heidi Gregory"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This marinade is good as a starter. I didn't have garlic powder on hand, so I added a teaspoon of minced garlic. I also added 1/4 cup of balsamic vinegar and a teaspoon of dry rib rub. Next time I will decrease the oil by half. All in all, not too bad.",
            "datePublished": "2016-07-30T20:26:18.890Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kimberly"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really good! A bit salty for us, next time I'll cut down on the soy and worster. Very tender pork chops on the BBQ!",
            "datePublished": "2012-07-18T23:25:33.460Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Christine T"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Simple, delicious, amazing!! I tweaked it with 5 packets of Splenda and let it marinade overnight and my pork chops were wonderful. I grilled them and my family loved them. And that includes two picky little children who just ate them up. Thanks for a great recipe.",
            "datePublished": "2004-09-21T16:49:19.193Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GottaEatAnyway"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I halved the recipe since I was only marinating 1 1/2 lb sirloin steak, and there was more then enough. The lightness of the lemon juice was a nice change for a beef dish and it had a good tenderizing effect after about 2 1/2 hours in the fridge. There were a lot of ingredients left up to \"taste\", so I just put in a TBL of McCormick Monterrey Steak Seasoning and it came out very well. When I use it for lighter meats, I'll use different spices, but it's definitely a keeper",
            "datePublished": "2009-04-19T05:41:46.290Z"
          },
          {
